== level 8 (Zagier E), s = 1/4, sigma(x) = x/(4x-1), y = 4x^2/(4x-1) ==
   Sigma_x = {0, 1/8, 1/4, oo}   (verified, 30_level16_involution.gp [2])
   fixed points of sigma: 0 (cusp) and 2s = 1/2 (NOT a cusp -> free point)
   Sigma_y = {0, -1/8, oo} punctures + CONE-2 at y = 4s = 1
   ceiling (fold image -1/8 dropped) = 64*|1| = 64.0  log = 4.158883083
   entry at the ceiling = -0.07657610031

== level 16, s = -1/4, sigma(x) = -x/(4x+1), y = 4x^2/(4x+1) ==
   Sigma_x = {0, -1/4, -1/2, (-1+-i)/4, oo}  (verified)
   sigma is induced by tau -> tau+1/2 (verified); fixed points 0 and 2s = -1/2,
   BOTH cusps  =>  the quotient carries NO cone point.
   Sigma_y = {0, -1/2, -1, oo}, all punctures; fold at y = oo,
             extra (outer pair) at y = -1/2, cusp x=2s at y = -1.
   drop the fold image y=oo        -> P^1-{0,-1/2,-1}       r = 16.0  log = 2.7725887  entry = -1.4628705
   drop the extra image y=-1/2     -> P^1-{0,-1,oo}         r = 16.0  log = 2.7725887  entry = -1.4628705
   drop y=-1 (image of cusp x=2s)  -> P^1-{0,-1/2,oo}       r = 8.0  log = 2.0794415  entry = -2.1560176
   drop nothing: P^1-{0,-1/2,-1,oo} = Y_0(8), y = 4q^2+...  r = 4.0  log = 1.3862944  entry = -2.8491648

   => under EITHER admissible choice of the single point phi may hit
      (the fold y=oo, or the extra point y=-1/2) the ceiling is exactly 16.
      The value 64 = 256|s| requires dropping BOTH y=-1/2 AND y=-1, i.e.
      pretending x=-1/2 is not a cusp.  It is one.

